    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find \\( t \\) in the polynomial equation \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) where the roots are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we will use Vieta's formulas which relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nGiven that \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) are the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), we apply Vieta's formulas again to this polynomial:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the sum of the roots of the new polynomial whose roots are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\). Using the property of symmetric sums, this sum is given by:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a+b+c)\n\\]\nSubstituting the value of \\( a+b+c \\):\n\\[\n2(a+b+c) = 2(-3) = -6\n\\]\n\nHence, the polynomial with roots \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\) is:\n\\[\nx^3 + r x^2 + s x + t = 0\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\nr = -(a+b) - (b+c) - (c+a) = (a+b+c) + (-a-b-c) + (-b-c-a) = (a+b+c) - (a+b+c) = 0 \\quad \\text{(non-critical information here)}\n\\]\n\\[\ns = -(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\n\\]\n\nNow, directly substituting it into the function \\( f(x) = x^3 + r x^2 + s x + t \\):\n\\[\nt = -((a+b)(b+c)(c+a))\n\\]\n\nBy using the identity for product of sums and symmetric properties of roots,\n\\[\nt = -(-504) = 504\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the constant term \\( t \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{504}\n\\]",
