      "text": "We use Vieta's formulas:\n\nFrom the first polynomial, by Vieta's formulas,\n\\[b + c + a = -3,\\quad ab + bc + ca = 4,\\quad abc = -11.\\]\n\nBy Vieta's formulas,\n\\[a + b + c = -r,\\quad ab + bc + ca = s,\\quad abc = -t.\\]\nThen, we can find $r$ and $t$ by adding together the sums of $a$, $b$, and $c$:\n\\[r = -(a + b + c) = 3,\\]\nand\n\\[s = ab + bc + ca = 4.\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[t = abc = \\boxed{-11}.\\]Conclusion:\n$a+b+c=a+(b+c)+(c+a)=-3+(a+b+c)=-3+3=0$",
